{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Repair round 1 for PR #33 (#17). Same rules as before: do not delegate further, stay on branch 17-claude, commit (new commits, no amend), do not push.\n\nStep 0 (REQUIRED): `git fetch && git rebase origin/main`. origin/main now has #16 (pi backend, e5d5d4e) and the fixtures PR. Resolve conflicts keeping both backends (enum arms, doctor sections, skill lines, models stubs: after #16 both pi and claude are implemented, so the \"not implemented\" skip path may disappear entirely). Study how #16 chooses and stores pi's `--session-id` before launch.\n\nREQUIRED fixes:\n1. Session id chosen before launch must be stored on the job (reuse #16's mechanism for pi), so a killed/cancelled claude run is resumable. Add an e2e assertion: cancel a claude run, then `resume` it and check the fake got `--resume <the same uuid>`.\n2. Pin the real `auto-refusal*.stdout` fixtures: assert their actual parse (is_error false, no permission_denials, text present) and comment that #6 recorded no refusal; keep the labelled synthetic denial test.\n3. One `Backend::ALL` constant (if #16 didn't add one) replacing duplicated backend lists in cli_info.rs / doctor.rs.\n4. Re-measure doctor locally (5 runs of `cargo test --test budgets`, note the max) and set DOCTOR_BUDGET_MS to ~1.5x the max observed, with the measurement in the comment.\n\nCUT-ONLY items (apply only if each removes lines; otherwise skip and say so):\na. `logged_in_flag`: parse `stdout.trim()` with serde_json into a struct with `loggedIn: bool`.\nb. Drop the `toolName` fallback in `denial_names` (keep `tool_name`).\nc. Replace `lenient_values` coercion with `#[serde(default)] Vec<Value>` for permission_denials.\nd. Replace hand-rolled `is_uuid` with a one-line shape check (no new dependency).\ne. One shared claude fake for tests via `include_str!` of a file under tests/ (e.g. tests/support/claude_fake.sh) instead of duplicated heredocs.\nf. `blank()` DoctorReport test builder → `Default` derives, only if shorter.\n\nGate: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test` all green. Report: commit SHA(s) + test counts, which cut-only items were applied/skipped, then Friction (≤3 bullets).\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}]},"session_id":"a6874d86-60bb-4e84-8f2b-a3973591ec9a"}
